			<h3>What is iDAL?</h3>
			<p>iDAL is a professional booking platform and community made for you. We created an alternative to the traditional model agency structure, providing a safe and efficient tool for you to work with clients directly.</p> 
			
			<h3>How does iDAL empower me?</h3>
			<p>On our platform, you make your own decisions on job offers, can negotiate your rate and receive payments while keeping track of all past, present and future projects and invoices. Before each booking you will receive a booking contract which has to be agreed to between you and the client. With iDAL, you also only pay 10% commission instead of the usual 20% - 40% and benefit from absolute financial transparency.</p>
			
			<h3>What is the iDAL community?</h3>
			<p>By joining iDAL, you become part of our community of entrepreneurial models in control of their careers. We are excited to have you and look forward to welcoming you and our other community members at our regular iDALVoices events. Through iDALVoices you can connect and collaborate, raise concerns and share your experiences in our online and offline spaces with fellow models, so that we can shape a better future for the modelling industry together.</p> 
			
			<h3>Who can be a model at iDAL?</h3>
			<p>iDAL is for entrepreneurial models - modelpreneurs. Those models who want to have full control over their careers and are business-savvy and proactive. </p>
			<p>Our models need to be over 18, have the right to work in the UK, have at least one professional portfolio image which reflects their talent, and present themselves professionally on social media. Our experienced managers verify each and every model before they appear on the iDAL talent page.</p>
			
			<h3>What makes iDAL different from a model agency?</h3>
			<p>iDAL does not act on behalf of Models or Clients. We do not promote individual models over others, do not select models for clients, and do not act as gatekeepers. Instead, we provide a safe and easy way for verified Models and Clients to connect and create projects together.</p>
			
			<h3>Who can see my profile on iDAL?</h3>
			<p>As we highly value safety your profile will only be visible to our verified clients & creatives.</p> 
			
			<h3>Who are the clients on iDAL?</h3>
			<p>iDAL accepts applications only from clients working in fashion, marketing and advertising industries. Every client goes through a thorough verification process which includes ID check. Today, we have clients ranging from luxury brands, to large fashion houses to upcoming designers.</p> 
			
			<h3>How do I get booked on iDAL?</h3>
			<p>If a client would like to cast or book you, they will request you on the platform. You will receive an email and an app notification when this happens. Make sure to enable your notifications!</p>
			<p>Once you receive an offer you will see all the details about the job in the job card. If you do not understand something, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@idal.co">support@idal.co</a>.</p> 
			
			<h3>What is the iDAL support number?</h3>
			<p>020 8187 7737</p>
			
			<h3>How do I negotiate on iDAL?</h3>
			<p>When you receive a booking on iDAL, you can see the proposed rate. If you think the rate is too low, you can negotiate the rate by clicking on the button ‘negotiate’. </p>
			
			<h3>How do I get paid on iDAL?</h3>
			<p>After you’ve worked with a client through iDAL, you will receive the payment directly to your bank account as soon as the client pays through iDAL. This usually happens within 7 to 30 days. Some companies may have a 60 day payment policy, should this be the case you will be notified.</p> 
			<p>We never hold your money unnecessarily, and our payment system pays out to you automatically as soon as the client pays. If you experience problems with the payment, please reach out at <a href="mailto:support@idal.co">support@idal.co</a>.</p>
			
			<h3>How much will I pay for the iDAL service?</h3>
			<p>We only charge 10% commission from you per booking.</p> 
			
			<h3>Can I contact clients through iDAL?</h3>
			<p>For safety reasons iDAL does not have direct messaging services with clients. Instead, our booking tools are designed to provide you with necessary information for your work. If you would like to know more about your job or a client, please reach out at <a href="mailto:support@idal.co">support@idal.co</a>.</p>
			
			<h3>Will I have a contract for a job booked through iDAL?</h3>
			<p>For each job request you will receive and have to agree to the booking terms directly with the client. You can find and read our <a href="/bookingterms">standardised service agreement here</a>. If you do not understand something in your contract, please get in touch with us at directly: <a href="mailto:support@idal.co">support@idal.co</a>.</p>
			
			<h3>Do I know the usage rights for jobs booked through iDAL?</h3>
			<p>You can view the requested usage rights under the project details of each booking.</p>
			
			<h3>What do I do if I think my usage rights were violated?</h3>
			<p>Please describe your concern in an email to <a href="mailto:support@idal.co">support@idal.co</a> and we will advise you regarding next steps.</p> 
			
			<h3>Why is booking through iDAL beneficial for clients?</h3>
			<p>On our transparent and easy-to-use platform, clients have direct access to talent, and all the necessary tools to cast and book models fast and transparently, all in one place, increasing their efficiency and cutting their costs.</p>
			
			<h3>What kind of safety does iDAL provide?</h3>
			<p>At iDAL we do our best to provide our members with a safe platform. That’s why we verify both our clients and models before either are able to access the platform and use our services. Furthermore, every booking is governed by our booking terms which both you and the client have to agree to before a booking can be finalised.</p> 
			
			<h3>Why is iDAL a more transparent service?</h3>
			<p>At iDAL we do not hide anything. No hidden fees, expenses, or small print in contracts. Transparent job offers, clients, rates, and commissions, all stored and easily accessible in one place.</p>
			
			<h3>Where can I find iDAL’s code of conduct?</h3>
			<p>Here: <a href="/conduct">https://idal.co/conduct</a>.</p>
			
			<h3>Who founded iDAL?</h3>
			<p>Mariya Grinina, a former journalist, and Tom Gordon, a full stack engineer with experience ranging from fintech to entertainment to fashion, realised the opportunity for technology to empower a positive change in the industry and launched iDAL in 2018.</p> 
				
